==English==
===Etymology===
{{etyl|enm}} {{term|manace|lang=enm}}, from {{etyl|xno}} {{term|manace|lang=fro}} 'threat', from {{etyl|la}} ''[[minacia]]'', from ''[[minax]]'' 'threatening', from ''[[minari]]'' 'to threaten, project', from {{proto|Indo-European|men-}} 'to project, stick out' (cf.  Old Norse {{term|mœna|lang=non}} 'to project', {{term|mœnir|lang=non}} 'ridgepole', Avestan fra''manyente'' 'they get a head start'). Related to [[mountain]].

===Noun===
{{en-noun|menaces}}

# a [[perceived]] [[threat]] or [[danger]]
# the act of [[threatening]]
# a [[dangerous]] person

===Verb===
{{en-verb|menaces|menacing|menaced}}  (''transitive'' or ''intransitive'')
# to make threats (against someone); to [[intimidate]]
# to [[endanger]] someone or something; to [[imperil]] or [[jeopardize]]

----

